    "created_at": "2026-11-21T10:31:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-21T10:31:55Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/3132-contour-none-lead · PR #3140 · pinned by arc_entry_with_both_leads_none_starts_the_cut_on_the_ring, plunge_entry_with_both_leads_none_starts_the_cut_on_the_ring, linear_and_arc_leads_keep_their_shapes, arc_entry_with_a_linear_lead_still_descends_on_its_arc · merges when reviewed\n\nCause: the Arc entry. With both leads None, its vertical wall arc runs about 8.7 mm back along the seam's tangent. From above, it looks like the linear lead. The fix stands the wall arc down when the lead-in is None. If the user's operation does not use the Arc entry, please reopen this issue with the entry type.\n",
